  "narrative": {
    "intro": "This ranking lists the largest federal contractors by contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Total obligations across all contractors in the table amount to $227B. OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. leads the list with $19.9B in obligations, followed by TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP with $13.7B, FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO with $13.4B, and MCKESSON CORPORATION with $11.1B. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION appears twice at $10.6B and $10.4B. ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION has $8.6B, RAYTHEON COMPANY has $8.1B, THE BOEING COMPANY has $5.9B, and BARNARD CONSTRUCTION COMPANY, INCORPORATED has $5.9B. The note on the page states that all figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date. Readers should treat the listed totals as partial obligations for FY2026 to date, not full fiscal year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which companies top the FY2026 obligations list?",
        "body": "OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. tops the list with $19.9B in obligations. TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP and FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO follow with $13.7B and $13.4B respectively. MCKESSON CORPORATION and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION are also among the highest, with $11.1B and entries at $10.6B and $10.4B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What does the $227B total represent?",
        "body": "The $227B figure represents total contract obligations for the entries shown, for FY2026 to date. The page note clarifies that these are partial totals, fiscal year to date, not full-year obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
